@startuml mtga-central-go-backend
title MTGA Central Go Platform - Components and Capacity Boundaries
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Desktop companion" as Desktop
actor "Operations user" as Operator

cloud "TLS ingress / CDN" as Edge
node "Stateless API replicas" as APIGroup {
  component "net/http API" as API
  component "Admission and policy" as Admission
  component "Manifest cache\nsmall and bounded" as Cache
}
node "Worker replicas" as WorkerGroup {
  component "Job poller" as Poller
  component "Bounded worker group" as Workers
  component "Catalog pipeline" as Catalog
  component "Telemetry aggregator" as Aggregator
}
database "PostgreSQL" as PG {
  component "Catalog metadata" as CatalogDB
  component "Consent and telemetry" as TelemetryDB
  component "Jobs, outbox and audit" as JobsDB
}
storage "Object storage" as Objects
cloud "Approved providers" as Providers
component "External secret store" as Secrets

Desktop --> Edge : HTTPS manifests and opt-in batches
Operator --> Edge : OIDC operations
Edge --> API
API --> Admission
Admission --> PG : pgxpool within replica budget
API --> Cache
Cache --> Objects : immutable artifacts
Poller --> JobsDB : lease with SKIP LOCKED
Poller --> Workers : bounded jobs
Workers --> Catalog
Workers --> Aggregator
Catalog --> Providers : limited fetches
Catalog --> CatalogDB : bounded batches
Catalog --> Objects : hash, verify, sign, publish
Aggregator --> TelemetryDB : idempotent aggregates
APIGroup ..> Secrets : runtime references
WorkerGroup ..> Secrets : signing and storage references

note bottom of APIGroup
  net/http already owns request goroutines.
  No detached post-response work.
end note
note bottom of WorkerGroup
  Context-owned goroutines, bounded channels,
  deterministic reducers and graceful drain.
end note
note bottom of PG
  Connection capacity sets API replicas,
  worker count and admission limits.
end note
@enduml
